@startuml
actor User
participant FE
participant BE
participant DB

User -> FE : Share file — enter recipient email\n+ own password\n+ optional: can_edit, expires_in_days

FE -> BE : POST /files/{id}/share\n{ recipient_email, password, can_edit, expires_in_days }\n[JWT in header]

BE -> BE : Validate JWT (must be file owner)

BE -> DB : Fetch file record + owner wrapped_FEK
DB --> BE : file record

BE -> DB : Fetch recipient user by email
DB --> BE : recipient record (id, public_key_pem)

BE -> DB : Fetch owner encrypted private key\n(private_key_enc, salt, nonce)
DB --> BE : encrypted private key blob

BE -> BE : Derive AES key from password\n(PBKDF2 + stored salt)
BE -> BE : Decrypt owner private key blob\n→ RSA private key object

BE -> BE : Unwrap FEK using owner\nRSA private key (OAEP)\n→ raw 32-byte FEK

BE -> BE : Re-wrap FEK using recipient\nRSA public key (OAEP)\n→ recipient_wrapped_FEK

BE -> DB : INSERT share record\n(\n  file_id,\n  owner_id,\n  recipient_id,\n  wrapped_fek = recipient_wrapped_FEK,\n  can_edit,\n  expires_at\n)
DB --> BE : OK

BE -> BE : Generate ID-based access link\n(file ID — no public token)
BE -> BE : [MOCK EMAIL] Print notification\nto server console

BE --> FE : 200 OK\n{ message, access_link, expires_at }
FE --> User : File shared successfully
@enduml
